WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.760
They were supposed to be safe in a country
that prides itself on being welcoming and

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:05.900
inclusive.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:10.580
But the massacres at two of their places of
worship have stunned the people of Christchurch.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:16.730
"It really hit home because I used to go to
that mosque, used to play there, hang out

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:22.310
there with my friends and stuff so seeing
that something like this has happened it almost

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:23.390
doesn’t feel real…

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:27.689
We thought islamophobia and xenophobia and
racism is something distant is something that

00:00:27.689 --> 00:00:30.520
happened in America and England.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:33.500
But it’s here and it is dangerous."

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:38.500
This center is providing information and psychological
support to friends and relatives who still

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:41.399
don’t know the fate of their loved ones.

00:00:41.399 --> 00:00:44.239
Sahra Ahmed is one of those awaiting news.

00:00:44.239 --> 00:00:47.219
She says the attacks will change New Zealand
forever.

00:00:47.219 --> 00:00:53.769
"I think what should change is the intelligence
gathering to spread out and not only focused

00:00:53.769 --> 00:01:02.001
on one community and it seems like security
has dropped the ball."

00:01:02.001 --> 00:01:04.900
The authorities here are still on high alert.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:09.920
This is one of the two mosques where dozens
were murdered as they met to pray on Friday

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:11.869
afternoon.

00:01:11.869 --> 00:01:17.930
"As you can see the scene has been heavily
cordoned off and police have warned other

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:23.720
mosques to keep doors closed for now.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:32.299
People here show how deeply that’s affected
people- talked to people who cried all night

00:01:32.299 --> 00:01:37.780
because they couldn’t believe something
like this could happen in New Zealand."

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:42.460
But A police warning for people to stay inside
couldn’t keep these residents of Christchurch

00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:52.369
from paying their respect to the Muslim victims
at a makeshift memorial.

00:01:52.369 --> 00:01:53.900
"Most people here aren’t from Muslim communities
because they don’t feel safe

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:55.900
we want to show that we support them."

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.000
"This is a city where people band together;

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.000
we've been through quakes together.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:07.000
This is just so far from the city that I know."

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:17.000
Today, Christchurch is in mourning and doubling down on its values as a multicultural society.

